G3992.def:
**πέμπω **
[in LXX chiefly for שָׁלַח ;]
**to send**;
(a) **of persons**: with accusative, absol., [[Mat.22.7|Mat.22:7]], [[Luk.7.19|Luk.7:19]], [[Jhn.1.22|Jhn.1:22]], [[2Co.9.3|2Co.9:3]], al.; ptcp. before verb., [[Mat.14.10|Mat.14:10]], [[Act.19.31|Act.19:31]], al.; ptcp. before διά (= _Heb._ יָד;, [[1Ki.16.20|1Ki.16:20]], al.), [[Mat.11.2|Mat.11:2]] (cf. [[Rev.1.1|Rev.1:1]]); of teachers sent by God, [[Jhn.1.33; 4.34|Jhn.1:33 4:34]], [[Rom.8.3|Rom.8:3]], al.; with accusative and dative, [[1Co.4.17|1Co.4:17]], [[Php.2.19|Php.2:19]]; before πρός, with accusative, [[Luk.4.26|Luk.4:26]], [[Jhn.16.7|Jhn.16:7]], al.; before λέγων (cf. _Heb._ אָמַר שָׁלַח [[Gen.38.25|Gen.38:25]], al.), [[Luk.7.6, 19|Luk.7:6, 19]]; before εἰς, with accusative loc., [[Mat.2.8|Mat.2:8]], [[Luk.15.15|Luk.15:15]], al.; before εἰς (of purpose), [[Eph.6.22|Eph.6:22]], [[Col.4.8|Col.4:8]], [[1Pe.2.14|1Pe.2:14]]; with inf., [[Jhn.1.33|Jhn.1:33]], [[1Co.16.3|1Co.16:3]], [[Rev.22.16|Rev.22:16]];
(b) **of things **: [[Rev.11.10|Rev.11:10]] before εἰς, [[Rev.1.11|Rev.1:11]] id., of purpose, [[Act.11.29|Act.11:29]], [[Php.4.16|Php.4:16]]; with dative of person(s), [[2Th.2.11|2Th.2:11]] π. τ. δρέπανον σου (cf. εξαποστείλατε δρέπανα = מַגָּל שָׁלַח, [[Jol.3.13|Jol.3:13]]), [[Rev.14.15, 18|Rev.14:15, 18]] (cf. ἀνα-, ἐκ-, μετα-, προ-, συν-πέμπω)
_SYN._: ἀποστέλλω, q.v (AS)

G3962.def:
**πατήρ**, πατρός, -τρί, τέρα, [in LXX chiefly and very frequently for אָב ;]
**a father**;
1. prop.,
(a) **of the male parent**: [[Mat.2.22|Mat.2:22]], [[Luk.1.17|Luk.1:17]], [[Jhn.4.53|Jhn.4:53]]; anarth., [[Heb.12.7|Heb.12:7]] (M, _Pr._, 82 f.); pl., of both parents (cl.), [[Heb.11.23|Heb.11:23]] οἱ π. τ. σαρκός, [[Heb.12.9|Heb.12:9]]
(b) **of a forefather or ancestor **(in cl. usually in pl.; Hom., al.): [[Mat.3.9|Mat.3:9]], [[Luk.1.73|Luk.1:73]], [[Jhn.8.39|Jhn.8:39]], al.; pl., [[Mat.23.30, 32|Mat.23:30, 32]] [[Luk.6.23, 26|Luk.6:23, 26]] [[Jhn.4.20|Jhn.4:20]], [[1Co.10.1|1Co.10:1]], al.
2. Metaphorical,
(a) **of an author, originator, or archetype **(= αἴτιος, ἀρχηγός, etc.; Pind., Plat., al.): [[Jhn.8.41-44|Jhn.8:41-44]], [[Rom.4.11, 12|Rom.4:11, 12]] 16.
(b) as a title of respect or honour, used of seniors, teachers and others in a position of responsible authority ([[Jdg.17.10|Jdg.17:10]], [[2Sa.2.12|2Ki.2:12]], [[Pro.1.8|Pro.1:8]], al.): [[Mat.23.9|Mat.23:9]] [[Act.7.2; 22.1|Act.7:2 22:1]], [[1Jn.2.13|1Jn.2:13]].
3. Of God (as in cl. of Zeus) as Father;
(a) **of created things**: τ. φώτων, [[Jas.1.17|Jas.1:17]]
(b) **of all sentient beings**: [[Eph.3.14, 15|Eph.3:14, 15]] [[Heb.12.9|Heb.12:9]];
(with) of men, esp. those in covenant relation with Him (freq in OT and later Jewish lit.; see Dalman, _Words_, 184ff.): [[Mat.6.4|Mat.6:4]], [[Luk.6.36|Luk.6:36]], [[Jhn.4.21|Jhn.4:21]], [[Jas.3.9|Jas.3:9]], al.; ὁ π. ὁ ἐν (τ.) οὐρανοῖς, [[Mat.5.16|Mat.5:16]], [[Mrk.11.25|Mrk.11:25]]; ὁ π. ὁ οὐράνιος, [[Mat.6.14; 15.13|Mat.6:14 15:13]]; esp. in the Epp., of Christians: [[Rom.8.15|Rom.8:15]], [[2Co.6.18|2Co.6:18]], [[Gal.4.6|Gal.4:6]], [[Eph.2.18; 4.6|Eph.2:18 4:6]], [[1Jn.2.1|1Jn.2:1]] with genitive qual., τ. οἰκτιρμῶν, [[2Co.1.3|2Co.1:3]] τ. δοξῆς, [[Eph.1.17|Eph.1:17]]
(d) **of Christ **(Dalman, _Words_, 190 ff.);
(α) **by our Lord himself**: ὁ π., [[Mat.11.25-27|Mat.11:25-27]], [[Luk.10.2, 22|Luk.10:2, 22]] [[Jhn.5.20-23|Jhn.5:20-23]], al.; ὁ π. μου, [[Mat.11.27|Mat.11:27]], al.; ὁ ἐν τ. οὐρανοῖς, [[Mat.7.11|Mat.7:11]], al.; ὁ οὐράνιος, [[Mat.15.13|Mat.15:13]] vocat., [[Jhn.11.41; 12.27, 28; 17.1, 5, 11, 20, 25|Jhn.11:41 12:27, 28 17:1, 5, 11, 20, 25]] (cf. Abbott, _JG_., 96 f.);
(β) **by Apostles**: [[Jhn.1.14|Jhn.1:14]] (anarth.; see M, _Pr._, l.with), [[Rom.15.6|Rom.15:6]], [[2Co.1.3; 11.31|2Co.1:3 11:31]], [[Eph.1.3|Eph.1:3]], [[Col.1.3|Col.1:3]], [[Heb.1.5|Heb.1:5]], [[1Pe.1.3|1Pe.1:3]], [[Rev.1.6|Rev.1:6]] (cf. Westc., _Epp. Jo._, 27-34).
(AS)

G3985.def:
**πειράζω ** poët. and late prose form of πειράω, which see,
[in LXX for נָסָה pi. ;]
1. to make proof of (Hom.).
2. to try, attempt (Luc., Polyb., with inf. (see M, _Pr._, 205; B1., § 69, 4), [[Act.9.26; 16.7; 24.6|Act.9:26 16:7 24:6]].
3. In LXX and NT, like _Heb._ נָסָה, with accusative of person(s), to test, try, prove;
(a) **in a good sense **: [[Jhn.6.6|Jhn.6:6]], [[2Co.13.5|2Co.13:5]], [[Heb.11.17|Heb.11:17]], [[Rev.2.2|Rev.2:2]]; esp. of trials and af6ictions sent or permitted by God ([[Gen.22.1|Gen.22:1]], [[Exo.20.20|Exo.20:20]], [[Wis.3.5|Wis.3:5]], al.), [[1Co.10.13|1Co.10:13]], [[Heb.2.18; 4.15; 11.17, 37|Heb.2:18 4:15 11:17, 37]], [[Rev.3.10|Rev.3:10]];
(b) **in a bad sense **(Apoll. Rhod., 3, 10): of the attempts made to ensnare Jesus in his speech, [[Mat.16.1; 19.3; 22.18, 35|Mat.16:1 19:3 22:18, 35]] [[Mrk.8.11; 10.2; 12.15|Mrk.8:11 10:2 12:15]], [[Luk.11.16|Luk.11:16]], [[Jhn.8.6|Jhn.8:6]]; of temptation to sin, to tempt, [[Jas.1.13-14|Jas.1:13-14]] (see Hort, in l), [[Gal.6.1|Gal.6:1]], [[Rev.2.10|Rev.2:10]]; esp. of temptations of the devil, [[Mat.4.1|Mat.4:1]], 3 [[Mrk.1.13|Mrk.1:13]], [[Luk.4.2|Luk.4:2]], [[1Co.7.5|1Co.7:5]], [[1Th.3.5|1Th.3:5]]; ὁ πειράζων, the tempter, [[Mat.4.3|Mat.4:3]], [[1Th.3.5|1Th.3:5]];
(with) in bad sense also ([[Exo.17.2|Exo.17:2]], 7, [[Num.14.22|Num.14:22]], al.), of distrustful testing, trying or challenging of God: [[Act.15.10|Act.15:10]], [[1Co.10.9|1Co.10:9]] (WH, mg., ἐξεπείρασαν), [[Heb.3.9|Heb.3:9]] τ. πνεῦμα Κυρίου, [[Act.5.9|Act.5:9]] (of. ἐκ-πειράζω).†
_SYN._: δοκιμάζω, q.v (AS)

G3958.def:
**πάσχω **
[in LXX: [[Amo.6.6|Amo.6:6]] (חָלָה ni.), [[Wis.12.27|Wis.12:27]], [[Sir.38.16|Sir.38:16]], al. ;]
to suffer, be acted on, as opposite to acting, often limited by a word expressive of good or evil;
(a) of misfortunes (most frequently without any limiting word) : absol., [[Luk.22.15; 24.46|Luk.22:15 24:46]], [[Act.1.3; 3.18; 17.3|Act.1:3 3:18 17:3]], [[1Co.12.26|1Co.12:26]], [[Heb.2.18; 9.26; 13.12|Heb.2:18 9:26 13:12]], [[1Pe.2.19-20; 2.23; 3.17; 4.15; 4.19|1Pe.2:19-20 2:23 3:17 4:15 4:19]]; before ὑπό, with genitive, [[Mat.17.12|Mat.17:12]] ὑπέρ, [[Act.9.16|Act.9:16]], [[Php.1.20|Php.1:20]], [[2Th.1.5|2Th.1:5]], [[1Pe.2.21|1Pe.2:21]]; with dative ref., [[1Pe.4.1|1Pe.4:1]] περί, with genitive (before ὑπέρ), [[1Pe.3.18|1Pe.3:18]] διά, with accusative, [[1Pe.3.14|1Pe.3:14]] ὀλίγον (a little while), [[1Pe.5.10|1Pe.5:10]] with accusative, [[Mat.27.19|Mat.27:19]], [[Mrk.9.12|Mrk.9:12]], [[Luk.13.2; 24.26|Luk.13:2 24:26]], [[Act.28.5|Act.28:5]], [[2Ti.1.12|2Ti.1:12]], [[Heb.5.8|Heb.5:8]], [[Rev.2.10|Rev.2:10]]; παθήματα, [[2Co.1.6|2Co.1:6]] ταῦτα, [[Gal.3.4|Gal.3:4]] (EV; cf. Lft., in l, but see infr.); accusative before ἀπό, [[Mat.16.21|Mat.16:21]], [[Luk.9.22; 17.25|Luk.9:22 17:25]]; ὑπό, [[Mrk.5.26|Mrk.5:26]], [[1Th.2.14|1Th.2:14]];
(b) of pleasant experiences (but always with qualifying word, εὖ or accusative of thing(s)) : [[Gal.3.4|Gal.3:4]] (cf. Grimm-Thayer, see word; Interp. Corn., in l, but see supr.) (cf. προ-, συν-πάσχω).†
(AS)

G3925.def:
**παρ-εμ-βολή**, -ῆς, ἡ
(παρεμβάλλω), [in LXX chiefly for מַחֲנֶה ;]
1. an insertion, interpolation (Æschin.)
2. In the Macedonian dialect (Rutherford, _NPhr._, 473), as a military term;
(a) **an army in battle array**: [[Heb.11.34|Heb.11:34]] (cf. [[Exo.14.19-20|Exo.14:19-20]], [[Jdg.4.16|Jdg.4:16]], al.; frequently in Polyb.);
(b) a camp ([[Exo.29.14|Exo.29:14]], al.) : [[Heb.13.11, 13|Heb.13:11, 13]] [[Rev.20.9|Rev.20:9]];
(with) **barracks, soldiers' quarters**: [[Act.21.34, 37; 22.24; 23.10, 16; 23.32; 28.16|Act.21:34, 37 22:24 23:10, 16 23:32 28:16]] (WH, txt., R, om.).†
παρ-εμ-βάλλω,
[in LXX frequently and chiefly for מַחֲנֶה ;]
1. to put in beside or between, interpose.
2. In late writers (Polyb., al., LXX) as technical military term;
(a) of soldiers, to draw up in line (frequently in [[1Ma.2.32|1Ma.2:32]], al.);
(b) **of siege works, to cast up**: with accusative and dative, χάρακά σοι, [[Luk.19.43|Luk.19:43]]†
(AS)
